{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.PairingParityForcesPositiveB3","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.PairingParityForcesPositiveB3","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PairingParityForcesPositiveB3.not_nonpos_of_pairing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PairingParityForcesPositiveB3.not_nonpos_of_pairing","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PairingParityForcesPositiveB3.lean#L102-L106","doc":"The contrapositive, as the falsifiable form: a mechanism whose `A = 2` value\nis negative and whose `A = 3` value vanishes **cannot** produce `b₃ ≤ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PairingParityForcesPositiveB3.pairing_sign_is_scale_free","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PairingParityForcesPositiveB3.pairing_sign_is_scale_free","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PairingParityForcesPositiveB3.lean#L93-L100","doc":"**The sign is independent of the magnitude.** Scaling `δ` scales the\ncontribution and cannot change its sign, so no choice of pairing strength can\nmake this mechanism give `b₃ ≤ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PairingParityForcesPositiveB3.pairing_b3_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PairingParityForcesPositiveB3.pairing_b3_eq","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PairingParityForcesPositiveB3.lean#L88-L91","doc":"The contribution stated exactly: `3δ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PairingParityForcesPositiveB3.pairing_forces_b3_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PairingParityForcesPositiveB3.pairing_forces_b3_pos","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PairingParityForcesPositiveB3.lean#L79-L86","doc":"**The pairing term forces `b₃ > 0`.** The deuteron is odd-odd, so pairing\nenters it as `−δ`; `A = 3` is odd-`A`, so pairing vanishes there. The resulting\ncontribution is `3δ`, positive for **every** `δ > 0` — the sign comes from the\nparities, not from the coefficient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PairingParityForcesPositiveB3.b3Contrib","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PairingParityForcesPositiveB3.b3Contrib","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PairingParityForcesPositiveB3.lean#L75-L77","doc":"The contribution of a term to the connected three-body cumulant, from its\nvalues at `A = 2` and `A = 3`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}